How can I help you, sir?

769
01:07:02.525 --> 01:07:05.259
I'm here to open
my safety deposit box.

770
01:07:05.261 --> 01:07:07.563
Okay.
What's the number on the box?

771
01:07:07.565 --> 01:07:14.603
Um, my dad, he gave me his keys
and told me to come here.

772
01:07:14.605 --> 01:07:15.770
And who's your father?

773
01:07:15.772 --> 01:07:17.838
David Earl Millings.

774
01:07:17.840 --> 01:07:19.310
What's your name?

775
01:07:21.344 --> 01:07:23.545
Russell.

776
01:07:23.547 --> 01:07:25.650
And you say
that you're his son.

777
01:07:27.951 --> 01:07:31.587
No, I didn't say I'm his son.

778
01:07:31.589 --> 01:07:33.824
I'm his son.

779
01:07:35.926 --> 01:07:38.196
Do you have an I.D.,
Mr. Millings?

780
01:07:48.572 --> 01:07:50.742
- Just give me one sec.
- Okay.

781
01:07:52.909 --> 01:07:55.212
Hey, Jim, can I see you
for a second?

782
01:07:58.382 --> 01:08:00.349
I think
there's a transient here.

783
01:08:00.351 --> 01:08:03.253
Has the key to one of our boxes.
Last name Millings.

784
01:08:07.391 --> 01:08:08.756
I'll get Joey
to get him out here.

785
01:08:08.758 --> 01:08:11.228
I'll take care of it.
Thank you.

786
01:08:16.967 --> 01:08:19.600
Here you go, Mr. Millings.

787
01:08:19.602 --> 01:08:21.903
I'm Jim Pitt, manager here.

788
01:08:21.905 --> 01:08:25.442
I am so sorry
for any misunderstandings.

789
01:08:31.815 --> 01:08:35.817
We were wondering
when you were gonna stop by.

790
01:08:35.819 --> 01:08:37.922
Your father, he was a...

791
01:08:39.757 --> 01:08:42.757
Well, he was a client here
for many years.

792
01:08:42.759 --> 01:08:44.462
Good man.

793
01:08:46.763 --> 01:08:49.400
Do you know
what's in our box?

794
01:08:51.634 --> 01:08:53.902
Right this way.

795
01:08:53.904 --> 01:08:56.641
It's just back here.
Jeannie.

796
01:09:07.750 --> 01:09:11.853
I'll give you
a few moments alone.

797
01:09:11.855 --> 01:09:15.793
When you need me, I'll be
right outside, Mr. Millings.

798
01:10:59.695 --> 01:11:06.467
<i>Son, I can only imagine
the road that you've traveled.</i>

799
01:11:06.469 --> 01:11:09.904
<i>I'm writing you
on New Year's Eve.</i>

800
01:11:09.906 --> 01:11:13.073
<i>Tomorrow is a new millennium,
a new decade,</i>

801
01:11:13.075 --> 01:11:17.445
<i>a new year, a new day.</i>

802
01:11:17.447 --> 01:11:19.747
<i>Folks are saying it's all
coming to an end</i>

803
01:11:19.749 --> 01:11:21.817
<i>with this Y2K shit,</i>

804
01:11:21.819 --> 01:11:24.219
<i>but I don't believe it.</i>

805
01:11:24.221 --> 01:11:28.155
<i>I think about
you a lot, Rusky.</i>

806
01:11:28.157 --> 01:11:31.596
<i>I imagine you in that prison.</i>

807
01:11:32.695 --> 01:11:36.500
<i>I try to take away
the world between us.</i>

808
01:11:37.834 --> 01:11:42.069
<i>And then I try to take
away the walls that hold you.</i>

809
01:11:42.071 --> 01:11:43.975
<i>And I see you...</i>

810
01:11:45.942 --> 01:11:47.576
<i>...asleep in your cell,</i>

811
01:11:47.578 --> 01:11:52.480
<i>hovering in the dark air,
alone.</i>

812
01:11:52.482 --> 01:11:55.649
<i>I call out your name
in the night.</i>

813
01:11:55.651 --> 01:11:58.855
<i>You will only ever be
my boy...</i>

814
01:12:03.026 --> 01:12:05.092
<i>...the guy I found
in your mother's arms</i>

815
01:12:05.094 --> 01:12:06.927
<i>that November afternoon.</i>

816
01:12:06.929 --> 01:12:09.898
<i>You were the happiest guy.</i>

817
01:12:09.900 --> 01:12:14.202
<i>The guy who shared everything
with everyone.</i>

818
01:12:14.204 --> 01:12:17.271
<i>The guy
who taught me how to love.</i>

819
01:12:17.273 --> 01:12:19.875
<i>I love you, Russ.</i>

820
01:12:19.877 --> 01:12:23.043
<i>So I'm giving them all
to you, Rusky.</i>

821
01:12:23.045 --> 01:12:27.015
<i>The Tyrian plum alone should
get you back on your feet.</i>

822
01:12:27.017 --> 01:12:29.783
<i>And your other key
is to a storage unit</i>

823
01:12:29.785 --> 01:12:31.019
<i>just down the street.</i>

824
01:12:31.021 --> 01:12:32.988
<i>Keep them, sell them.</i>

825
01:12:32.990 --> 01:12:37.094
<i>Just find your way, Russell.</i>

826
01:12:41.197 --> 01:12:45.300
<i>It's a second chance
after such a bad hand.</i>

827
01:12:45.302 --> 01:12:48.769
<i>Go see the world, son.</i>

828
01:12:48.771 --> 01:12:50.941
<i>Don't look back, buddy.</i>

829
01:12:52.709 --> 01:12:54.175
<i>Your mother used to say,</i>

830
01:12:54.177 --> 01:12:55.877
<i>"Once in a while,
it hits people</i>

831
01:12:55.879 --> 01:12:58.046
<i>that they don't
have to experience the world</i>

832
01:12:58.048 --> 01:13:00.015
<i>in the way
they have been told to."</i>

833
01:13:00.017 --> 01:13:01.616
<i>Ha ha!</i>

834
01:13:01.618 --> 01:13:03.955
<i>Smartest girl I ever met.</i>

835
01:13:05.821 --> 01:13:08.689
<i>I love you, son.</i>

836
01:13:08.691 --> 01:13:14.895
<i>That can't change the past,
but the past can't change that.</i>

837
01:13:14.897 --> 01:13:19.234
<i>I love you like a wolf
loves the moon.</i>

838
01:13:21.004 --> 01:13:25.006
<i>Love, Mom, Dad.</i>

839
01:14:06.717 --> 01:14:08.149
Hi, Mr. Millings.

840
01:14:08.151 --> 01:14:09.951
Good to see you again.
How can I help you?

841
01:14:09.953 --> 01:14:11.952
I was here
to check on Ella.

842
01:14:11.954 --> 01:14:15.090
Yes, I did get
all of your e-mails.

843
01:14:15.092 --> 01:14:16.824
Ella is doing great,

844
01:14:16.826 --> 01:14:19.894
and we have yet to be contacted
by any of her relatives,

845
01:14:19.896 --> 01:14:23.030
but she is thriving in
a temporary home right now.

846
01:14:24.200 --> 01:14:27.270
Thanks.
That's... yeah.

847
01:14:28.338 --> 01:14:32.107
I looked into
the adoption process.

848
01:14:32.109 --> 01:14:33.241
- Yes.
- Remember...

849
01:14:33.243 --> 01:14:35.010
Okay, listen.

850
01:14:35.012 --> 01:14:37.945
I'm gonna be completely frank
with you, Mr. Millings.

851
01:14:37.947 --> 01:14:40.881
You are going to have
a tough go at it.

852
01:14:40.883 --> 01:14:42.716
I'm not saying
it's impossible.

853
01:14:42.718 --> 01:14:46.887
Do you know, I realize that's
unlikely, you know, that...

854
01:14:46.889 --> 01:14:48.390
I mean, that's not
why I'm here.

855
01:14:48.392 --> 01:14:51.696
I'm here
to give this to you.

856
01:14:52.995 --> 01:14:55.095
It's for Ella.

857
01:14:55.097 --> 01:14:56.331
Okay?

858
01:14:56.333 --> 01:14:59.000
And if you could
give it to her

859
01:14:59.002 --> 01:15:02.706
on her 18th birthday, okay?

860
01:15:05.808 --> 01:15:08.409
Wait, why her 18th birthday?

861
01:15:08.411 --> 01:15:10.278
'Cause that's the way
the trust was set up.

862
01:15:10.280 --> 01:15:11.746
That's what they said.

863
01:15:11.748 --> 01:15:13.247
That way
it would be just for her,

864
01:15:13.249 --> 01:15:15.216
and she would be ready.

865
01:15:15.218 --> 01:15:18.153
Can you make sure
that she gets it?

866
01:15:18.155 --> 01:15:19.688
- Yeah, o-of course.
- Okay.

867
01:15:19.690 --> 01:15:21.221
I sent all this to you
in a e-mail

868
01:15:21.223 --> 01:15:24.693
with information about the trust
and instructions.

869
01:15:24.695 --> 01:15:28.930
And it's best if you leave
the envelope i-in the plastic.

870
01:15:28.932 --> 01:15:31.035
It protects the stamps.

871
01:15:32.268 --> 01:15:34.204
Oh... Thank you.

872
01:15:48.118 --> 01:15:49.717
- Have a nice trip.
- Thank you.

873
01:15:49.719 --> 01:15:51.121
Mm-hmm.

874
01:15:53.155 --> 01:15:54.424
Next.

875
01:16:01.130 --> 01:16:02.463
Where would
you like to go, sir?

876
01:16:02.465 --> 01:16:05.002
Mm...
